  "limitations": [
    "RUN-04 retains admission digest and source-key ownership, RUN-01 retains the primary Run lifecycle, and RUN-05 retains action-key, action-state, connector-receipt, and dispatch persistence; ORCH-07 composes their receipts and extracts only the stale recovery decision policy.",
    "Webhook, scheduler, and manual API transports remain responsible for producing stable source event IDs and invoking the validator before this service; their endpoint and occurrence receipts belong to their dedicated requirements.",
    "The current catalog hash is a constructor-captured trusted composition snapshot; the composition root must rebuild the receipt service whenever it installs a new catalog release.",
    "ORCH-09 owns redacted audit append and will compose through receive_in_uow so its initial receipt event shares this transaction without duplicating on replay.",
    "The recovery policy preserves RUN-05 deterministic durable-mock guarantees and honest outcome-unknown behavior; it does not claim universal exactly-once delivery from external providers."
  ]
